---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { BRAND_NAME } from "../lib/brand";
import {
  getBreadcrumbSchema,
  resolveSiteUrl,
} from "../lib/schemaMarkup";

const siteUrl = resolveSiteUrl(Astro.site);
const schema = [
  getBreadcrumbSchema(siteUrl, [
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Terms of service", path: "/terms" },
  ]),
];
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of service"
  description={`${BRAND_NAME} terms: web and Android clients, accounts, sensor data license, billing via Stripe, monitoring disclaimer, and liability limits.`}
  schema={schema}
>
  <article class="card max-w-3xl mx-auto my-8">
    <h1 class="card-title">Terms of service</h1>
    <p class="card-subtitle">
      Simple terms for using ThermalTrace (website, PWA, and Android app). Last updated August 29, 2026.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">The service</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      ThermalTrace provides dashboards, history, alerts, and integrations for temperature and related
      sensor data you connect—via the website, Progressive Web App, and the Android companion app.
      Features depend on your plan (Free, Member, Pro). We may change, suspend, or discontinue features
      with reasonable notice when practical.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Clients &amp; devices</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      The Android app and PWA are clients for your ThermalTrace account. They do not replace probe
      hardware: temperature and humidity come from sensors or feeds you configure. Optional push alerts
      (browser Web Push and Firebase Cloud Messaging on Android) require a Pro plan where noted and
      depend on OS/network delivery outside our control.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Your account</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      You are responsible for credentials, device keys, and household invites you create. Keep ingest
      keys private. Do not abuse the APIs, scrape aggressively, or attempt to access other users’ data.
      We may suspend accounts that threaten service stability or other customers.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Your data &amp; sensors</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      You own the readings and configuration you submit. You grant us a limited license to store and
      process that data to run the product (charts, alerts, exports, backups, push delivery). See the
      <a class="text-link" href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for retention and deletion.
      You are responsible for how you place sensors and for acting on alerts — ThermalTrace is a
      monitoring aid, not a life-safety or building-code compliance system.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Billing</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Paid plans are billed through Stripe. Fees, trials, and cancellations follow the checkout and
      customer portal flows. The Pro trial is free; cancel before it ends and you are not charged.
      After conversion to a paid plan, the current billing period is generally non-refundable.
      Taxes may apply. Failure to pay may reduce your account to Free limits.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Open source &amp; trademarks</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      Application source may be available under its repository license. The ThermalTrace name and
      branding are ours; using the software does not grant trademark rights.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Disclaimer</h2>
    <p class="text-sm">
      The service is provided “as is.” We do not warrant uninterrupted uptime or that alerts will
      always arrive before damage occurs. To the fullest extent allowed by law, ThermalTrace and its
      operators are not liable for indirect, incidental, or consequential damages (including property
      loss from freeze, heat, flood, or outage). Our total liability for a claim is limited to fees
      you paid us for the service in the three months before the claim.
    </p>

    <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6 mb-2">Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-0">
      Questions about these terms:
      <a class="text-link" href="/contact">contact form</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
